1	//! Guardian review decides whether an `on-request` approval should be granted
2	//! automatically instead of shown to the user.
3	//!
4	//! High-level approach:
5	//! 1. Reconstruct a compact transcript that preserves user intent plus the most
6	//!    relevant recent assistant and tool context.
7	//! 2. Ask a dedicated guardian review session to assess the exact planned
8	//!    action and return strict JSON.
9	//!    The guardian clones the parent config, so it inherits any managed
10	//!    network proxy / allowlist that the parent turn already had.
11	//! 3. Fail closed on timeout, execution failure, or malformed output.
12	//! 4. Approve only low- and medium-risk actions (`risk_score < 80`).
